  "id": "Compound::DB06209 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Prasugrel, a direct-acting antithrombotic drug, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three paths indicating that Cyp2c19 participates in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, a key enzyme in the oxidation of limonene. The shared pathway from Prasugrel to Cyp2c19 to Cyp2c9 suggests a mechanistic link where Prasugrel may inhibit the activity of Cyp2c9, potentially affecting the metabolism of its substrates. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, reliable relationship, supported by the common biological role of Cyp2c9 in metabolic processes. The evidence suggests that Prasugrel may act as a competitive inhibitor of Cyp2c9, thereby modulating its activity in the context of drug metabolism.",
